Z||000000||Gus||09-19-2001||11:45 PM||||Been reading this forum for a few days now I found good tech.info and good humor so I joined. <P>With info from Will and jay I decided to go simple and strong.  So I bought a used 93 NorthStar engine $300.00 CDN had 80,000 ks from a freind who just didn't have the time to build his own. going to bolt a carb intake with 850 cfm carb,Electromotive HPV-1 ignition system, mod cams all form Cadillac HotRod Fabricators , and getrag 5 speed. <P>Take this combo and raise it into my 87 GT probably a good thing we have long winter in Canada. We'll se how it goes.  <P>Did I mention I was going to try do this complete for less than $6,000.00 CDN. Hmmm<P>                      GGIII||||reg||6
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||09-19-2001||11:51 PM||||I'll be the first to say:  Welcome to the Forum!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Also, best of luck to ya with the N*  I'm curious to find out how you're going to get the getrag 5spd on it, since it is my understanding (from reading on here) that the N* won't work with a manual.  If it works, and especially for under $6000 CDN, it might get my interest back.  My V8 swap is still 2 years away, but I'm still trying to decide between LT1 and N*.  Be sure to take lots of pics of your work!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
