Z||000006||Jay||09-22-2001||03:27 PM||||Hey Gus, glad you joined.  I think you're making a mistake about going with carbs.  I've found someone that can do the programming of the eprom so you won't throw codes and it should be pretty cheap (In comparison to changing over to carbs).  This way you can retain stock ECM.  I did my conversion complete with rims and interior for under $10 000 Canadian so your target of $6000 should be right on.  Do as much of the work yourself and save big time.  Let me know if you need any help.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
