Z||000010||artherd||09-23-2001||02:09 AM||||Hi Gus, Welcome!!!<P>The Northstar does indeed bolt up (after you tweak some things a bit, it's easy and can be done with a $50 tool in 20min.)<P>The proof is in the pudding, here's some!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/northstar1.jpg"> <P>I have to ask about the carb though, it seems a pity to take such a marvel of technology, and saddle it with a hundred-year throwback.<P>Why not use the Holley Commander 950 ECU also from Chrfab?  The electromotive product is also a computer, with DIS you're basically stuck either way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>All that said, it's your bloody car and you're going to do as you like!! (and I hope you pick the route you want and will be happiest with.  That's why we have these cars, they make us grin like idoits!!!)<P>Oh, Also, Jay and Will may have a way to use the stock ECU with a new PROM chip, give them a hollar.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
